<style>
/* K · Cormorant Garamond with Jost. Announcement bar, one-row header. Menus: capital text columns with a photograph flush right. Two buttons under the intro. */
:root{--display:"Cormorant Garamond",Georgia,serif;--sans:"Jost",system-ui,sans-serif}
.logo{font-size:32px;font-weight:600}
.nav{margin-left:clamp(36px,4vw,64px);gap:clamp(18px,2vw,30px)}
.hero-copy h1{font:600 clamp(38px,3.8vw,60px)/1.02 var(--display)}
.hide-d{display:none}
@media (max-width:1080px){.hide-d{display:inline-flex}}
.sp + .ws{padding-top:0}
.sp:has(+ .ws){padding-bottom:clamp(40px,4vw,56px)}
.bh + .sp-size{padding-top:0}
.sp-size + .pv-k{padding-top:0}
.sp-size:has(+ .pv-k){padding-bottom:clamp(40px,4vw,56px)}
.pv-k + .rv{padding-top:clamp(40px,4vw,56px)}
.pv-k + .bd2{padding-top:0}
.bd2 + .rv{padding-top:0}
.rv.r1 .cards{align-items:stretch}
.rv.r1 .cd{border-top:0;padding-top:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100%}
.rv.r1 .cd .rq{flex:1}
/* one rhythm: every section below the hero sits the same distance apart */
:root{--sec:clamp(56px,6vw,88px)}
main > section:not(.hero):not(.next){padding-top:0!important;padding-bottom:0!important;margin-top:var(--sec)!important;margin-bottom:0!important}
main > section.next{margin-top:var(--sec)}
</style>

<div class="dw lg"><header class="dw-hero"><div class="dw-w"><nav class="dz-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/pages/help">Help</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Privacy policy</span></nav><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>How we collect, use and look after your personal information, and the rights you have over it.</p><p class="lg-upd">Last updated 12 November 2026</p></div></header><div class="dw-body dw-w"><aside class="dw-side"><div class="dw-on"><span>On this page</span><a href="#who">Who we are</a><a href="#collect">What we collect</a><a href="#use">How we use it</a><a href="#share">Who we share it with</a><a href="#keep">How long we keep it</a><a href="#rights">Your rights</a><a href="#complain">Making a complaint</a><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></div></aside><div class="dw-main"><section id="who"><h2>Who we are</h2><p>This website is run by Axel &amp; Hound Ltd, a company registered in England and Wales (company number [00000000]), with its registered office at [address]. We are the controller of your personal data, which means we decide how it is used and are responsible for keeping it safe.</p><p>If you have any questions about this policy or your data, email us at [hello@axelandhound.co.uk].</p></section><section id="collect"><h2>What we collect</h2><p>We only collect what we need to run the shop and look after you:</p><ul class="dw-notes"><li>Your name, email address, phone number and delivery and billing addresses, when you place an order or create an account.</li><li>Your order history, returns and any messages you send us.</li><li>Payment details, which are handled securely by our payment providers. We never see or store your full card number.</li><li>Information about how you use our website, such as pages viewed and the device you use, collected through cookies if you agree to them.</li><li>Your dog&rsquo;s name and size, if you choose to tell us, to help with sizing.</li></ul></section><section id="use"><h2>How we use it</h2><div class="dw-tw"><div class="dw-tw"><table class="dw-tb "><thead><tr><th scope="col">Why we use it</th><th scope="col">Our lawful basis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Why we use it">To process, deliver and support your order, including returns and refunds</th><td data-l="Our lawful basis"><span>Performing our contract with you</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Why we use it">To send emails about your order, such as confirmations and tracking</th><td data-l="Our lawful basis"><span>Performing our contract with you</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Why we use it">To send our newsletter and offers, if you sign up</th><td data-l="Our lawful basis"><span>Your consent, which you can withdraw at any time</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Why we use it">To prevent fraud and keep our website secure</th><td data-l="Our lawful basis"><span>Our legitimate interests</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" data-l="Why we use it">To keep records for tax and accounting</th><td data-l="Our lawful basis"><span>Legal obligation</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section id="share"><h2>Who we share it with</h2><p>We never sell your data. We share it only with companies that help us run the shop, and only as much as they need:</p><ul class="dw-notes"><li>Shopify, which hosts our website and stores order information.</li><li>Payment providers, including Shopify Payments, PayPal, Klarna and Apple Pay.</li><li>Delivery couriers, so they can deliver your order.</li><li>Our email provider, to send order updates and, if you&rsquo;ve agreed, our newsletter.</li><li>Trustpilot, if you leave a review.</li></ul><p>Some of these companies are based outside the UK. Where your data is transferred abroad, we make sure it is protected by appropriate safeguards, such as the UK International Data Transfer Agreement.</p></section><section id="keep"><h2>How long we keep it</h2><p>We keep order records for six years, as required for tax purposes. Account details are kept until you close your account. Newsletter details are kept until you unsubscribe. After that, your data is deleted or made anonymous.</p></section><section id="rights"><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Under UK data protection law, you have the right to:</p><ul class="dw-notes"><li>See a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li><li>Ask us to correct anything that is wrong or incomplete.</li><li>Ask us to delete your data, where we no longer need to keep it.</li><li>Object to, or ask us to limit, how we use your data.</li><li>Ask for your data in a format you can take elsewhere.</li><li>Withdraw your consent to marketing at any time, using the unsubscribe link in any email.</li></ul><p>To use any of these rights, email [hello@axelandhound.co.uk]. We will reply within one month.</p></section><section id="complain"><h2>Making a complaint</h2><p>If you&rsquo;re unhappy with how we&rsquo;ve handled your data, please tell us first so we can put it right. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner&rsquo;s Office (ICO) at ico.org.uk or on 0303 123 1113.</p></section><section id="changes"><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p></section><section class="dw-help"><h2>Still need help?</h2><p>Our team is here Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm, and replies to every message within one working day.</p><a class="dw-btn" href="/pages/contact">Contact us</a></section></div></div></div>


